["PRECONDITION (Tier-A gate): a daily bias / direction must already be established before the checklist is applied — 'once I have a daily bias or Direction I will use this checklist to make sure all requirements are met before I take an entry'.", "CHECKLIST STEP 1 — STOP RAID: a prior low must be put in and then raided/broken (liquidity sweep) — 'the first thing I focus on is a stop raid this just means that a low was put in before it was rated or broken'.", "CHECKLIST STEP 2 — MARKET STRUCTURE SHIFT / DISPLACEMENT: a previous high is broken and aggressively moved through — 'a previous high was broken and aggressively moved over'.", "FILTER (sequencing gate): the displacement must be PRECEDED by a stop raid; a displacement with no prior (lower-timeframe) liquidity raid is rejected — 'I prefer to have a stop rate prior to the displacement so I am not counting this as a displacement move up' and 'without a lower time frame liquidity rate prior to a move I am not interested in it'.", "CHECKLIST STEP 3 — RETURN TO DISCOUNT: after displacement, wait for price to retrace back into the DISCOUNT of the displacement range; do not enter (long) above the 0.5 — 'I'd want to be longing this green section down here' / 'I'm not looking too long Above This 0.5'. (Flexibility acknowledged: 'where there is a little bit flexibility'.)", "OTE REFINEMENT: an OTE (optimal trade entry) fib narrows the discount zone — premium above is a no-long area, the OTE marks the refined discount entry band — 'using an OTE ... this is our premium up here where I do not want to be longing and this Narrows down my discount range to my OTE'.", "CHECKLIST STEP 4 — PD ARRAY at the point of interest; taught variants: FAIR VALUE GAP (preferred), ORDER BLOCK (preferred), OTE, BREAKER BLOCK — 'some sort of PD array where generally I prefer to have a fair value gut or an order block but I will also use an OTE ... as well as a breaker block'. Order block = a down-close candle (for shorts) / breaker block = the up-close candles before the liquidity raid.", "BOX-SETUP VARIANT SUB-MECHANIC: a deviation/manipulation out of the range (aggressive move down then aggressive move up = accumulation/manipulation) → wait for a RETEST of that manipulation → target the OTHER SIDE of the range — 'this is the deviation from the range and so accumulation manipulation I want to see distribution so ideally I'm looking for a retest of this manipulation to then be reaching for the other side'. Explicitly does NOT require a prior structure shift — 'although we did not shift structure prior to this entry this is a box setup entry'.", "SELECTION / BLEND rule: each concept can be used as an entry model by itself OR 1-3 concepts blended together — 'each one of these Concepts could be used as an entry model by themselves however I like to blend one two or three of these Concepts together'; examples: FVG within an OTE, box setup within an OTE, FVG nested inside an order block that lines up with the box setup.", "ENTRY-SELECTION by RISK-TO-REWARD (executable core): moving the entry closer to the stop increases R:R but raises no-fill risk; balance R:R against getting filled — 'as I move my entry closer to my stop loss my risk to reward increases however the further I go there is also the possibility that I do not get filled'.", "DISCOUNT/PREMIUM FILTER on the PD array: reject a PD array (e.g. an FVG) that sits in the PREMIUM of the range for a long — 'does that meet all my criteria it does not because it is in a premium of the range'.", "ENTRY: enter at the chosen PD array (FVG / order block / breaker block / OTE / box-setup retest), e.g. 'for my entry I would personally be looking to enter the trade right here', 'my entry would be on this order block', 'from here we have order block fair value Gap so I would be looking to enter here'.", "STOP — the taught ORDER-BLOCK stop: stop on the order block — order-block HIGH for a short ('my stop on the order block High'), order-block LOW for a long ('putting my stop on this order block low'); or on the swept structure low ('My Stop on this low').", "TARGET: opposite-side liquidity — buy-side liquidity above for longs ('looking for buy side liquidity up here'), a new low / sell-side for shorts ('targeting a new low'), 'the other side' for the box setup, or the initial highs from the morning ('target the initial highs from the morning').", "MANAGEMENT: take a first partial at the nearer liquidity, then move stop to break-even, then let runners run to the further liquidity — 'first partial here', 'if I move my stop to break even', 'partial or move my stop to break even your target the initial highs ... and from there let runners run'.", "OCCURRENCE TOLERANCE: a single tick beyond the low is not counted as invalidating the level — 'we did go a tick below this low but I do not count that personally'."]

